🟠 ledger in billing (prod-eu-1) keeps running out of memory. Its registry is healthy and unchanged, so nothing outside it points to a cause. It was killed at its 512Mi memory limit; it used 500Mi at peak in the last 24 hours. Its last run lasted two hours; four restarts since its pod was created one hour ago. Fix in: deployment/ledger → container app → resources.limits.memory (512Mi). To read the output of the last crash, run kubectl logs ledger-c10ffc84-a -c app -n billing --previous
